Phrase 4. A BIT OF ANALYSIS:
a) main verb: volo;
b) 1st infinitive clause object: scire... etc.; whose subject understood is that of the main clause: Congrio;
c) completive clause object of scire: utrum sinas an non sinas (= utrum sinas annon); this clause is moreover interrogative (introduced by utrum);
d) infinitive clause (complete) object of sinas (annon): nos coquere hic cenam. Note that in this last one hic is not the demonstrative adjective pronoun but the demonstrative adverb of place (question ubi?) of the 1st person (there where I am).
